## 3. Obstruction report — what blocks A1

**First unresolved statement.** The literal joint one-loop numerator

```
N_{μν}(p) = N^Wilson_{μν}(p) + N^FP_{μν}(p) + N^Haar_{μν}(p)
```

of Bałaban, *CMP* **109** (1987) 249–301 (beta extraction (5.36)–(5.42)) is not
constructed here, and consequently neither of the two bounds it must satisfy —
`|Π(p)| ≤ (1/40) p̂²` on the near box and `|Π(p)| ≤ 25/128` on the far shell —
is proved. Everything downstream of those two inequalities is now machine-checked;
nothing upstream of them is.

Why it was not constructed in this round: writing the three channel numerators
*literally* requires the lattice Feynman rules of the source (the Wilson
three-gluon and four-gluon vertices at the relevant momentum routing, the reduced
Faddeev–Popov determinant in the same gauge-fixing convention, and the Haar
measure counterterm normalisation). Those are transcription-from-source items,
and the source text is not available in this environment. Writing down a
plausible-looking vertex from memory and calling it "the CMP109 integrand" would
be a fabricated provenance claim, not a derivation, so it was not done. The
honest statement is: **A1a is closed modulo a single, precisely stated scalar
inequality about an object that still has to be transcribed or re-derived from
the lattice Feynman rules.**

**Second unresolved statement (A1b).** The actual observer coordinates
`O_β(K)`, the actual contraction factor `κ` and the actual Lipschitz constant
`L_β` of the shell coefficient on the physical small-field tube are not derived.
The package proves what those constants *buy* (uniformly in shells, with the
fallback for the non-pointwise case, and with the `κ = 1` boundary shown to
fail), but the constants themselves require the explicit Balaban block-spin
step. No numerical value of `κ` or `L_β` is claimed.

**Consequently: no Clay leaf is closed by this round, and the official count
stays at 5.** The Yang–Mills existence and mass-gap theorem is not proved here,
and nothing in this repository should be read as proving it.

